// Simple type value write and read, vector elements always have fld=0.
// All these types are passed by value instead of by reference.
//
// @FR-H-ReadNull / @FR-H-WriteNull / @FR-H-WriteOOB — every accessor below opens with the
// SAME test, `rec == 0`, because a target that names no live cell has one spelling: an index
// out of range answers `nullref` (@FR-H-Index) and so does a keyed miss or an unfilled field.
// A getter answers its type's null sentinel; a setter does nothing and the program continues,
// so a write can never resolve a store for an absent target and scribble at record 0.  These
// bodies are the SHARED half of the two backends — the interpreter's `fill.rs` arm and the
// native emitter both carry this text — which is why the two agree here by construction
// rather than by test.  (The lock half of the write rule, @FR-H-WriteLocked, is not tested
// here: it lives one level down in `Store::addr_mut`.)
